{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The remaining data variables `N`, `M`, and `X` are context inputs. Each parameter has exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before it is used in the likelihood.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N; // Number of data
  int<lower=1> M; // Number of covariates
  matrix[M, N] X;
  array[N] real y;
}

parameters {
  vector[M] beta;
  real alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

model {
  // Strongly regularizing priors
  beta ~ double_exponential(0, 1);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 2);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 2);

  y ~ normal(X' * beta + alpha, sigma);
}
